<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan invites bids for export of rice.</title>
<headline>Pakistan invites bids for export of rice.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Rice Export Corporation of Pakistan said on Thursday it had invited bids by December 24 for the sale and export of 40,000 to 45,000 tonnes of IRRI-6 variety rice.  </p>
<p>Javed Islam Agha, chairman of the private Rice Exporters Association of Pakistan, said Iraq was likely to take part in the bidding following its oil-for-food deal with the United Nations.</p>
<p>Agha said the long-grain IRRI-6 Sindh white rice containing 10 percent broken would be sold from stocks held by the Rice Export Corporation of Pakistan.</p>
<p>The corporation's move marked its re-entry into the export market after a gap of several weeks.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
